<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>News from Asia-Pacific - Latest headlines and news reports - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage of political, social and geostrategic issues across Asia and the Pacific, including those affecting China, Japan, South Korea, North Korea, India, Pakistan and Australia.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/</link><lastBuildDate>Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:46:09 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>Typhoon Champi batters Taiwan</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/typhoon-champi-batters-taiwan</link><description>
Typhoon Champi is heading towards China and Japan. Yesterday, it battered Taiwan with heavy rain and winds reaching up to 180 kilometres per hour. Across the island, 56,000 households are without power. Nicolas Chamontin and Ophelie Jacobson report.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f59c94bc-cf95-11f1-8d18-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261024-121303-121445-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f59c94bc-cf95-11f1-8d18-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261024-121303-121445-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fab3c510-cf95-11f1-b25f-45bbb0637d0b</guid><pubDate>Sat, 24 Oct 2026 10:33:04 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The 51%</category><title>Why do women in public life become targets?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261023-why-do-women-in-public-life-become-targets</link><description>
A brutal targeted attack on an Australian female MP, who lost both her legs as a result, has reignited concerns over the rising levels of violence against women in public life. Also Cornell University is facing a no-confidence vote over its handling of an alleged gang rape in 2024. Annette Young speaks to Annie E. Clark, a survivor of campus sexual assault and Dr Sara Wilf of George Mason University about why institutions continue to struggle with sexual assault cases.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5908bff4-ceeb-11f1-8d64-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-PKG-HELEN-HAINES-ATTACK-BEN-BRAHIM-Jennifer.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5908bff4-ceeb-11f1-8d64-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-PKG-HELEN-HAINES-ATTACK-BEN-BRAHIM-Jennifer.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2b3d0958-cee7-11f1-bf03-a7cbd5a932b9</guid><pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 13:58:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Annette YOUNG</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>Singapore's longevity industry: The quest for eternal youth</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261023-singapore-s-longevity-industry-the-quest-for-eternal-youth</link><description>
In Singapore, the quest for eternal youth is no longer just a billionaire's fantasy. It's becoming big business. High-tech clinics, longevity labs and specialist companies all promise the same thing: slowing down the ageing process. From continuous metabolic monitoring and genetic testing to supplements and oxygen therapy, every aspect of the body is measured and optimised.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5859209e-ced7-11f1-9bf9-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-63ab9de4.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5859209e-ced7-11f1-9bf9-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-63ab9de4.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d4a9fb60-ce31-11f1-8981-ebbb528b1ec1</guid><pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 11:53:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Théo Collet</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Taiwan shuts down schools and businesses as Typhoon Champi approaches</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261023-taiwan-shuts-down-schools-and-businesses-as-typhoon-champi-approaches</link><description>
As Typhoon Champi approached Taiwan, most businesses and schools were closed across the island Friday and hundreds of flights were canceled in the region. Authorities reported at least one death and dozens of injuries and more than 1,200 people have evacuated their homes.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5c2df22-ce8d-11f1-90c0-1da646a5f16c/w:1024/p:16x9/d819a05d5c2fe530ae3991168d68541f32c11897.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5c2df22-ce8d-11f1-90c0-1da646a5f16c/w:1024/p:16x9/d819a05d5c2fe530ae3991168d68541f32c11897.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f6bb5544-ce8d-11f1-a482-a9d16325b13a</guid><pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 03:00:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5c2df22-ce8d-11f1-90c0-1da646a5f16c/w:1024/p:16x9/d819a05d5c2fe530ae3991168d68541f32c11897.jpg">© I-Hwa Cheng, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Strong earthquake strikes China’s remote Tibet region</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261022-many-dead-massive-earthquake-strikes-china-s-remote-tibet-region-magnitude-seven</link><description>
At least 16 people have died and dozens more injured after a major earthquake measuring 7.0 on the Richter scale shook China’s remote Tibet region on Thursday, state media said. Hundreds of houses collapsed in the tremor.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d9d92e24-ce5b-11f1-9517-7967b15eed96/w:1024/p:16x9/2025-08-20T063420Z-1364597011-MT1SPYC0622927-RTRMADP-3-SCIENCE-PHOTO-LIBRARY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d9d92e24-ce5b-11f1-9517-7967b15eed96/w:1024/p:16x9/2025-08-20T063420Z-1364597011-MT1SPYC0622927-RTRMADP-3-SCIENCE-PHOTO-LIBRARY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cf26565e-ce5c-11f1-a38e-315ede859882</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 21:09:38 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d9d92e24-ce5b-11f1-9517-7967b15eed96/w:1024/p:16x9/2025-08-20T063420Z-1364597011-MT1SPYC0622927-RTRMADP-3-SCIENCE-PHOTO-LIBRARY.jpg">© Science Photo Library via Reuter/ Illustration picture</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Tête à tête</category><title>Dalai Lama appointed by China 'is going to be a fake one', exiled former Tibetan leader says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261022-dalai-lama-appointed-by-china-is-going-to-be-a-fake-one-exiled-former-tibetan-leader-says</link><description>
In an interview with FRANCE 24, exiled former Tibetan leader Lobsang Sangay said any successor to the Dalai Lama appointed by China "is going to be a fake one". He also likened Beijing's ethnic unity law to "an ethnic erasure", said Tibetan concerns had been "downgraded a bit" in US-China talks and accused China of failing to warn of the deadly August floods on the Nepal-Tibet border.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bbc18672-c7b5-11f1-a05b-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-PKG-CLEAN-TETE-A-TETE-Lobsang-Sangay-AUBIN-Sophian.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bbc18672-c7b5-11f1-a05b-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-PKG-CLEAN-TETE-A-TETE-Lobsang-Sangay-AUBIN-Sophian.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ecb91a8e-c7b4-11f1-bd29-9f686ef585fa</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 10:22:48 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marc PERELMAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Down to Earth</category><title>Indonesia continues to battle wildfires, with nearly 2 million hectares burned</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/down-to-earth/20261020-indonesia-continues-to-battle-wildfires-with-nearly-2-million-hectares-burned</link><description>
Fires in Indonesia have burned through more than 1.9 million hectares of land, according to new data, as the country battles its worst wildfire season in a decade. The blazes have sent toxic smoke across much of Southeast Asia, forcing schools to close and fuelling a rise in respiratory illnesses. FRANCE 24's Environment Editor Valerie Dekimpe tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7692e870-cbcf-11f1-aae0-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/202610191145AS-ASIA-WEATHERINDONESIA-WILDFIRE-VOLUNTEE-O.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7692e870-cbcf-11f1-aae0-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/202610191145AS-ASIA-WEATHERINDONESIA-WILDFIRE-VOLUNTEE-O.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2fbedfe4-cbd4-11f1-b5e6-1b78e86d5641</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:23:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Valérie DEKIMPE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Driver charged over 'targeted' car attack on Australian lawmaker Helen Haines</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261020-driver-charged-over-targeted-car-attack-on-australian-lawmaker-helen-haines</link><description>
Police on Tuesday charged a driver with intentionally causing serious injury to Australian federal lawmaker Helen Haines, who is in a critical condition after being struck by a car outside her office in an incident that has shocked the nation. Haines had her leg amputated following the attack, according to Australian media reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f6683382-cc12-11f1-96de-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/c1c8c1ea21994ca7557dedaa39af9ec3e387267a.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f6683382-cc12-11f1-96de-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/c1c8c1ea21994ca7557dedaa39af9ec3e387267a.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">76975eea-cc2f-11f1-83c9-a5bedbad9e99</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 02:39:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f6683382-cc12-11f1-96de-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/c1c8c1ea21994ca7557dedaa39af9ec3e387267a.jpg">© William West, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Months-long Indonesia wildfires spew toxic haze across Southeast Asia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261018-months-long-indonesia-wildfires-spew-toxic-haze-across-southeast-asia</link><description>
Parts of southern Southeast Asia have been put under the highest-level haze alert as wildfires that have swept Indonesia for months continue to belch toxic smoke across the region. The seasonal wildfires are worse this year due to the drought conditions caused by a severe "super-El Nino" effect.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/959c6e42-cab9-11f1-bcc1-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-25T172531Z-1337943422-RC29QNASKLJ4-RTRMADP-3-ASIA-WEATHER-INDONESIA-WILDFIRE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/959c6e42-cab9-11f1-bcc1-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-25T172531Z-1337943422-RC29QNASKLJ4-RTRMADP-3-ASIA-WEATHER-INDONESIA-WILDFIRE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e45050c0-caba-11f1-85b5-bd1110e119fe</guid><pubDate>Sun, 18 Oct 2026 06:30:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/959c6e42-cab9-11f1-bcc1-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-25T172531Z-1337943422-RC29QNASKLJ4-RTRMADP-3-ASIA-WEATHER-INDONESIA-WILDFIRE.jpg">© Abriansyah Liberto, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>India's 'cockroach' movement founder released from police custody</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261018-india-s-cockroach-movement-founder-released-from-police-custody</link><description>
Indian police released Cockroach Janta Party (CJP) founder Abhijeet Dipke from detention on Saturday after the activist was detained ahead of a rally calling for the resignation of India's chief election commissioner. Two other CJP leaders remain in custody after having been arrested while demonstrating at a protest site that police had ruled off-limits.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b8ff30cc-cab4-11f1-8c54-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3KJ7R8.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b8ff30cc-cab4-11f1-8c54-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3KJ7R8.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6df91d22-cab4-11f1-9715-9b17793e8591</guid><pubDate>Sun, 18 Oct 2026 05:47:00 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b8ff30cc-cab4-11f1-8c54-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3KJ7R8.jpg">© Arun Sankar, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Access Asia</category><title>Indonesia's forest fires spark public health crisis across Southeast Asia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261016-indonesia-s-forest-fires-spark-public-health-crisis-across-southeast-asia</link><description>
Massive wildfires in Indonesia show no sign of letting up. The environmental disaster is turning into a pollution crisis across Southeast Asia, as toxic haze from the blazes spread to neighbouring countries. 
 
 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ff39c682-c961-11f1-a160-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3DA3TF.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ff39c682-c961-11f1-a160-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3DA3TF.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8f0453c2-c958-11f1-b7e7-97512286b526</guid><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 15:26:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Yuka ROYER</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Indian authorities detain 'cockroach' movement founder Dipke ahead of new protest</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261016-indian-authorities-heighten-security-close-park-ahead-cockroach-movement-rally</link><description>
Indian authorities on Friday detained Abhijeet Dipke, the founder of the satirical youth movement "Cockroach Janta Party", ahead of a new protest in New Delhi, live images from the group showed. Police earlier closed a central New Delhi park in an attempt to stifle near-daily demonstrations calling for the election authority chief's resignation over the removal of more than 130 million people from voter lists.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b8a2bfba-c927-11f1-8e00-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26288364408466.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b8a2bfba-c927-11f1-8e00-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26288364408466.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ca4a6fd8-c927-11f1-be75-15e1c7afe358</guid><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 06:39:48 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b8a2bfba-c927-11f1-8e00-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26288364408466.jpg">© Manish Swarup, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Pakistan school roof collapse kills dozens of pupils, teacher in Peshawar</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261015-pakistan-school-roof-collapse-kills-dozens-of-pupils-teacher-in-peshawar</link><description>
A teacher and at least 32 pupils were killed when a school roof collapsed in the northwestern Pakistani city of Peshawar on Thursday, authorities said. At least twenty people were injured, three of them severely.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/aa866466-c86b-11f1-b34b-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26288241083154.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/aa866466-c86b-11f1-b34b-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26288241083154.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cdedae32-c86b-11f1-b21a-b9600c1a13aa</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 08:02:53 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/aa866466-c86b-11f1-b34b-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26288241083154.jpg">© Maaz Awan, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>North Korea test-fires submarine-launched cruise missiles amid rising tensions</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261014-north-korea-test-fires-submarine-launched-cruise-missiles</link><description>
North Korea test-fired two types of submarine-launched strategic cruise missiles on Wednesday, state media KCNA reported Thursday, saying the launches posed no threat to neighbouring countries. The tests follow heightened tensions with South Korea after a September 21 landmine explosion in the Demilitarised Zone injured three South Korean soldiers.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f1a9b998-c874-11f1-be54-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26288165399294-2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f1a9b998-c874-11f1-be54-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26288165399294-2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f99eab7c-c81a-11f1-9cc8-0b7b5cc63c30</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:12:08 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f1a9b998-c874-11f1-be54-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26288165399294-2.jpg">KCNA via KNS via AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>How far will 'Cockroach' movement go? India's youth-led protests defy Modi government</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261014-how-far-will-cockroach-movement-go-india-s-youth-led-protests-defy-modi-government</link><description>
It all started as a bit of online satire by a few young people fed up by corruption. Clearly though, the "Cockroach" movement is no longer a laughing matter for India’s government, which has shut transport and blocked rallying points in the capital to quell the momentum of a youth-led mobilisation that's already brought down the education minister over rampant school exam cheating and is now spearheading the protests against the culling of names from voter rolls, with the electoral commission chief accused of bias. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4239fb0a-c7fa-11f1-89b9-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-14T115755Z-850024491-RC2W2OARH6QL-RTRMADP-3-INDIA-POLITICS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4239fb0a-c7fa-11f1-89b9-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-14T115755Z-850024491-RC2W2OARH6QL-RTRMADP-3-INDIA-POLITICS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f84dcb48-c7f9-11f1-bdd4-9b1a8aad7837</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:40:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>‘The idea that Modi must be feared because he holds all levers of power has gone out of the window’</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/the-idea-that-modi-must-be-feared-because-he-holds-all-levers-of-power-has-gone-out-of-the-window</link><description>
Is Narendra Modi losing his most powerful political asset: the perception of invincibility? As India's youth protest movement confronts an increasingly combative government, Dr. Subir Sinha, Director of the SOAS South Asia Institute and Reader in Development Studies, argues that the political significance of the demonstrations extends far beyond the arrests of opposition activists and the growing confrontation between protesters and state institutions. Dr. Sinha examines how the government's increasingly repressive response may be exposing the fragility of its authority and institutional legitimacy. Could India's emerging protest movement be dismantling the political mythology that has sustained Modi's hold on power?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/54831ad4-c7e2-11f1-aba3-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-151217-152427-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/54831ad4-c7e2-11f1-aba3-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-151217-152427-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5984c96a-c7e2-11f1-8726-872246178d56</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:51:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Cheap weapons, growing fears: Inside the Taliban’s drone campaign against Pakistan</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261014-taliban-suicide-drone-attacks-pakistan</link><description>
Pakistan says it intercepted 23 suicide drones launched from Afghanistan into Pakistani airspace in September alone. Since the conflict began in February 2026, the Taliban have increasingly used drones to attack Pakistan, raising concerns in Islamabad.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5f545c36-c7b3-11f1-a790-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/Taliban-drones.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5f545c36-c7b3-11f1-a790-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/Taliban-drones.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">864651f8-c7b5-11f1-9790-cf719f7bbb72</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:52:44 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5f545c36-c7b3-11f1-a790-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/Taliban-drones.jpg">© Observers</source><dc:creator>Ershad ALIJANI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>‘Dark day for Turkey’: Police halt broadcasts, make arrests in raid on opposition TV</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261014-dark-day-for-turkey-pro-opposition-tv-channel-boss-slams-police-raid-broadcast-halt</link><description>
Turkish authorities appointed a government trustee to run popular broadcaster Halk TV on Wednesday after police raided its headquarters, halting live broadcasts and arresting 11 people. Halk chairman Cafer Mahirogluin denounced "a dark day for Turkey", adding that seven of his family members were among those detained. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/50cd18f0-c7aa-11f1-a852-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8E939G.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/50cd18f0-c7aa-11f1-a852-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8E939G.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d96c4b90-c7aa-11f1-a542-495be6bd29bc</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 09:09:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/50cd18f0-c7aa-11f1-a852-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8E939G.jpg">© Adem Altan, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>Asia's fertility hub: Thailand emerges as top destination for IVF treatment</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261013-asia-s-fertility-hub-thailand-emerges-as-top-destination-for-ivf-treatment</link><description>
Thailand has become one of Asia's leading fertility hubs. Every year, thousands of foreign patients travel to Bangkok's state-of-the-art private clinics for IVF, egg donation and other fertility treatments. They come from China, South Korea, Europe and across Southeast Asia, looking for what may be harder to find at home: shorter waiting times, lower costs and, in some cases, fewer restrictions.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/61cf2b02-c700-11f1-a4c1-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-20524719326ace21e3b0b017-95189063.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/61cf2b02-c700-11f1-a4c1-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-20524719326ace21e3b0b017-95189063.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4a557732-c661-11f1-9911-cbeaa347c34d</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:38:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Théo Collet</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>India’s youth-led Cockroach movement defies protest ban</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/india-s-youth-led-cockroach-movement-defies-protest-ban</link><description>
India’s youth-led Cockroach movement is intensifying protests against Prime Minister Narendra Modi’s government. Three leaders were detained after defying a ban at New Delhi’s Jantar Mantar protest site. Demonstrators are challenging a voter-list revision they claim favours Modi’s party, while the protests disrupt businesses across the capital.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4b962c40-c6f2-11f1-b580-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-120704-120853-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4b962c40-c6f2-11f1-b580-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-120704-120853-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">50936e10-c6f2-11f1-8188-45191249cb5c</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 11:00:18 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Thousands of Indians march to Supreme Court to oust election chief</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/thousands-of-indians-march-to-supreme-court-to-oust-election-chief</link><description>
Protesters in New Delhi continue to take to the streets demanding the country's top election commissioner resign. Frustrations have been mounting after an investigation in a leading newspaper revealed concerns had been raised within the body, over the revision of voter lists. Delano D'Souza reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1039adec-c658-11f1-8eee-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-161323-161506-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1039adec-c658-11f1-8eee-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-161323-161506-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1737a1e4-c658-11f1-ba0d-a1d59b7450e1</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:23:06 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>India's opposition leader marches with thousands against election chief</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/india-s-opposition-leader-marches-with-thousands-against-election-chief</link><description>
Opposition parties and supporters of the so-called "cockroach" youth movement marched towards the country's Supreme Court on Monday, in the latest show of outrage against the recent removal of millions of names from voters lists. Critics say the move is likely to benefit Prime Minister Narendra Modi's ruling party – and are demanding India's election chief step down over what they describe as misconduct. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in New Delhi, Navodita Kumari.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8f28789e-c645-11f1-bd3c-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-151704-152046-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8f28789e-c645-11f1-bd3c-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-151704-152046-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">94b8223c-c645-11f1-aaef-7d0d3890fc1a</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:14:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Five people missing as fresh flash floods hit central Nepal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261012-five-people-missing-as-fresh-flash-floods-hit-central-nepal</link><description>
Nepali rescuers searched for five missing people on Monday, a day after new flash floods swept away more than 200 houses and five bridges along the Budhi Gandaki River. The country is still recovering from devastating floods, triggered by a mountain glacial collapse on August 26, which killed more than 1,400 people and left over 5,000 missing.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5e4303c0-c64a-11f1-ac09-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/mininepal-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5e4303c0-c64a-11f1-ac09-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/mininepal-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">77e4b17a-c64a-11f1-9c6d-cdf17c4bf6b7</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:43:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Striking images show new flash floods hitting central Nepal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/striking-images-show-new-flash-floods-hitting-central-nepal</link><description>
Striking new images show new flash floods hitting central Nepal. This comes only six weeks after another disaster there left more than 1,400 dead and 5,000 missing. According to an initial assessment by the Nepalese authorities, at least five people are now missing. Elitsa Gadeva and France 2 have the details.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3071e9c6-c630-11f1-b345-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-101155-101324-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3071e9c6-c630-11f1-b345-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-101155-101324-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">356b36a8-c630-11f1-90dd-bd2c6267270e</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:14:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Press Review</category><title>'Illegal detentions' in India, as protesters allege foul play at Electoral Commission</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261012-illegal-detentions-in-india-as-protesters-allege-foul-play-at-electoral-commission</link><description>
PRESS REVIEW – Monday, October 12: Widespread protests in India are met with detentions judged "illegal" by the country's Supreme Court. But first: Lebanese papers report as Hezbollah prepares for a new regional flare-up. Finally, Citroën hopes to win hearts and minds with an electric reboot of the vintage Deux Chevaux model.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e1435126-c613-11f1-ad84-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-16135980746acc951abe4389-94721040.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e1435126-c613-11f1-ad84-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-16135980746acc951abe4389-94721040.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">39342392-c614-11f1-b994-bbd096d2ec97</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:51:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Antonia KERRIGAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Opposition leaders and journalists allege police abuses as fresh protests break out in India</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261012-opposition-leaders-and-journalists-allege-police-abuses-as-fresh-protests-break-out-in-india</link><description>
Indian opposition politicians and journalists alleged that police had been heavy-handed in cracking down in protests that swept New Delhi over the weekend in response to a nationwide voter roll revision that critics say disproportionately affects Muslim and other minority voters. Opposition leader Rahul Gandhi called for a fresh march to the nation's Supreme Court Monday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e8fae4d2-c592-11f1-ba7c-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/072cac240b0437489ebe812b6bc4c7d2b7354c07.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e8fae4d2-c592-11f1-ba7c-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/072cac240b0437489ebe812b6bc4c7d2b7354c07.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1a30a880-c5f6-11f1-ad03-25c042bca3a1</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 04:33:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e8fae4d2-c592-11f1-ba7c-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/072cac240b0437489ebe812b6bc4c7d2b7354c07.jpg">© Sajjad Hussain, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Melbourne Islamic leader denies links to suspected FlyDubai hijacker</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261012-melbourne-man-linked-to-suspected-flydubai-hijacker-condemns-false-accusations</link><description>
Abu Hamza, whose Melbourne-based Islamic community centre was linked by Emirati prosecutors to the suspect in the attempted hijacking of an Israel-bound passenger jet, publicly dismissed "false accusations" against him on Monday. While prosecutors alleged that the Omani co-pilot first became radicalised while studying in Australia, neither the community centre nor Hamza are accused of any criminal wrongdoing. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f2f3b51a-c5ef-11f1-b3c8-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/7dea89d7eb26f796afc2c3352cdc34dee3b5cd7e.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f2f3b51a-c5ef-11f1-b3c8-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/7dea89d7eb26f796afc2c3352cdc34dee3b5cd7e.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f43ea4c0-c5ef-11f1-85ce-c9e446fa1b4a</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 03:49:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f2f3b51a-c5ef-11f1-b3c8-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/7dea89d7eb26f796afc2c3352cdc34dee3b5cd7e.jpg">© Jack Guez, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>North Korea fires multiple ballistic missiles off east coast, Seoul says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261012-north-korea-ballistic-missiles-sea-japan-seoul</link><description>
North Korea fired multiple ballistic missiles off its east coast on Monday, South Korea’s military said, amid tensions over border landmine explosions that injured three South Korean soldiers last month. Seoul said the missiles were launched from Pyongyang and increased surveillance, while Japan confirmed at least one suspected ballistic missile.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d3d5e108-bed3-11f1-8d0c-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/33573f643956faa9ed06abffc2ea828d225eaae2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d3d5e108-bed3-11f1-8d0c-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/33573f643956faa9ed06abffc2ea828d225eaae2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">994097f0-c5df-11f1-bc10-e5e71626e698</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 01:54:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d3d5e108-bed3-11f1-8d0c-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/33573f643956faa9ed06abffc2ea828d225eaae2.jpg">© Philip Fong, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>India court orders release of 'cockroach' movement leaders after detention</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261011-india-court-orders-release-of-cockroach-movement-leaders-after-detention</link><description>
An Indian court ordered the release of three leaders of the viral "cockroach" youth movement on Sunday, a day after their detention ahead of protests over alleged irregularities in voter-roll revisions. Upon his release, founder Abhijeet Dipke called Narendra Modi an "embarassment to India" in a social media post.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d80c366e-c536-11f1-8938-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D22W7VJ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d80c366e-c536-11f1-8938-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D22W7VJ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6ce53ff2-c536-11f1-a177-bb862c9a8e61</guid><pubDate>Sun, 11 Oct 2026 05:45:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d80c366e-c536-11f1-8938-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D22W7VJ.jpg">© Indranil Mukherjee, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>India detains 'cockroach' leaders ahead of election protest</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261010-india-detains-cockroach-leaders-ahead-of-election-protest</link><description>
Indian police detained the head of the satirical "cockroach" online movement on Saturday, the group said, ahead of a major protest against the Election Commission that triggered strict security measures. Our correspondent Navodita Kumari tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1b855ea2-c483-11f1-a9b2-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261010-100108-100645-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1b855ea2-c483-11f1-a9b2-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261010-100108-100645-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">208b5a5a-c483-11f1-a48c-6d26eb27a2bd</guid><pubDate>Sat, 10 Oct 2026 09:18:11 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
